# Keep the build context to what the image is actually built from.
#
# bin/ and obj/ are the important ones and not for speed: the restore layer writes the container's
# own obj/, and copying the host's over it replaces an assets file that points at paths inside the
# image with one that points at paths on somebody's laptop. The publish then cannot find a single
# package it just restored.

**/bin/
**/obj/

.git/
.github/
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/

backups/
ops/releases/
docs/
tests/

**/*.user
**/.DS_Store
compose.yaml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
